    "body": "Honestly I think _subSequence_ or _innerSequence_ would be a better name. It's confusing to use the variable name _tuple_ for something that's actually an Infra list/IDL sequence.\r\n\r\nFor example, at first I wrote a comment below \"Why not just append _tuple_ directly, instead of appending (_tuple_[0], _tuple_[1])?\" But now I see that would be a type error. I was misled by the variable name.",
